      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'd settle for a good fallback rendering for these characters, but sometimes it's more complicated than it seems to block blank characters, because sometimes blank characters exist to fulfil a specific purpose in a specific language. I remember trying to block all non-printing characters once, and then getting a support request from a user (I think it was Arabic but actually can't clearly remember that part) who was unable to enter their name using the proper Unicode.",
